140
00:06:19.720 --> 00:06:22.500
that it doesn't look in the projection like
these are the actually

141
00:06:22.500 --> 00:06:24.280
nearest neighbors. But remember,
we're trying to

142
00:06:24.280 --> 00:06:28.440
squash down many, many higher dimensions
into this two-dimensional representation. So it's

143
00:06:28.440 --> 00:06:29.660
not always going to
be perfect.

144
00:06:29.780 --> 00:06:31.280
But the important thing
is to basically look

145
00:06:31.280 --> 00:06:33.500
at the structure of these results.
And you can see some

146
00:06:33.500 --> 00:06:37.040
are more outlier than others.
And this is actually the

147
00:06:37.040 --> 00:06:39.120
heart of the entire issue.

148
00:06:39.320 --> 00:06:41.500
The embedding model that
we use to embed

149
00:06:41.500 --> 00:06:43.920
queries and embed our
data does not have

150
00:06:43.920 --> 00:06:46.580
any knowledge of the
task or query we're

151
00:06:46.580 --> 00:06:49.580
trying to answer at the time we actually
retrieve the information.

152
00:06:49.760 --> 00:06:51.840
So the reason that
a retrieval system may

153
00:06:51.840 --> 00:06:54.660
not perform the way
that we expect is because we're

154
00:06:54.660 --> 00:06:57.220
asking it to perform
a specific task using

155
00:06:57.220 --> 00:06:59.160
only a general representation.

156
00:06:59.340 --> 00:07:00.800
And that makes things more complicated.

157
00:07:00.800 --> 00:07:03.958
Let's try visualizing a couple other
queries in a similar way. So

158
00:07:03.958 --> 00:07:07.116
here I'm just going to copy-paste the whole
thing. But the query

159
00:07:07.116 --> 00:07:10.226
now is what's the strategy around
artificial intelligence, that

160
00:07:10.226 --> 00:07:11.829
is AI. So
let's run and see what

161
00:07:11.829 --> 00:07:14.648
results we get. You see here that AI
is mentioned in most

162
00:07:14.648 --> 00:07:15.620
of these documents.

163
00:07:15.620 --> 00:07:18.060
And this is sort
of vaguely related to AI.

164
00:07:18.340 --> 00:07:21.020
We have a commitment
to responsible AI development.

165
00:07:21.180 --> 00:07:24.200
But then we have something about
this information about

166
00:07:24.200 --> 00:07:27.220
a database which is not directly
related to AI. And here we're

167
00:07:27.220 --> 00:07:29.720
talking about mixed reality
applications and metaverse, which

168
00:07:29.720 --> 00:07:32.960
is tangentially related
to technology investments, but

169
00:07:32.960 --> 00:07:35.840
not necessarily directly
AI related. So let's visualize.

170
00:07:36.020 --> 00:07:38.980
First, we'll project the same way as
we did in previous query.

171
00:07:39.980 --> 00:07:44.020
query. And then we will plot.

172
00:07:46.860 --> 00:07:47.540
Let's take a look.

173
00:07:47.980 --> 00:07:49.860
Here's
our query and our related results. And

174
00:07:49.860 --> 00:07:52.400
they're all coming from the same part
of the data set.

175
00:07:52.580 --> 00:07:54.380
But you can see that some
of the results that we get,

176
00:07:54.380 --> 00:07:56.340
you know, and here,
this point appears to be

177
00:07:56.340 --> 00:07:59.680
bang on where our query landed.
So it's super, super relevant. So

178
00:07:59.680 --> 00:08:02.060
you can see that, obviously, there's
where the query lands in

179
00:08:02.060 --> 00:08:03.840
the space has geometric
meaning and we're pulling in

180
00:08:03.840 --> 00:08:08.520
related results. But again, what's
related is from the general purpose embedding

181
00:08:08.520 --> 00:08:11.720
model, not from the specific
tasks that we're performing. So let's take

182
00:08:11.720 --> 00:08:12.880
a look at another
query.

183
00:08:12.980 --> 00:08:14.900
What has been the
investment in research and

184
00:08:14.900 --> 00:08:16.380
development?
This is a very general query,

185
00:08:16.380 --> 00:08:18.220
and it should be
reflected in the annual statement.

186
00:08:18.220 --> 00:08:20.120
So let's see what kind of
documents we get back. We

187
00:08:20.120 --> 00:08:23.660
see that we start with
general ideas about investments.

188
00:08:23.980 --> 00:08:25.840
Some of it is
about research and development.

189
00:08:25.840 --> 00:08:28.120
For example, this document,
research and development expenses,

190
00:08:28.120 --> 00:08:30.620
