development and programming costs.

191
00:08:30.740 --> 00:08:34.260
But we see that there
are also distractors in this result.

192
00:08:34.260 --> 00:08:38.530
So a distractor is a result that is
not actually relevant to the query,

193
00:08:38.530 --> 00:08:41.700
and it's called a distractor because
if you pass this

194
00:08:41.700 --> 00:08:44.260
information to the large
language model to complete

195
00:08:44.260 --> 00:08:46.820
your RAG loop, the
model tends to get distracted by

196
00:08:46.820 --> 00:08:49.360
this information and
output suboptimal results. And

197
00:08:49.360 --> 00:08:51.120
the reason this is
really important is that

198
00:08:51.120 --> 00:08:53.980
bad behavior from the
model due to distractors

199
00:08:53.980 --> 00:08:56.860
is very difficult to
diagnose and debug, both

200
00:08:56.860 --> 00:08:59.620
for the user, but also for developers
and engineers building

201
00:08:59.620 --> 00:09:00.720
these types of systems.

202
00:09:01.040 --> 00:09:04.640
So it's very important to make your retrieval
system robust and

203
00:09:04.640 --> 00:09:08.240
return relevant results and no distracting
results to the model.

204
00:09:08.600 --> 00:09:10.900
So again, let's
take a look at the projection. I

205
00:09:10.900 --> 00:09:13.000
always find it very, very
helpful to visualize.

206
00:09:13.840 --> 00:09:16.840
And again, because this is a
